From 050e2366a6e20d86c4e3eab2e2a95f4ca0ce384f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@cern.ch>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 20:29:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix: Make statistics dependencies optional at import time

* bin/CheckMATE imports checkmate_core at top level, which until now
unconditionally imported the five multi-bin/likelihood statistics
modules and thereby required pyhf, matplotlib, jsonpatch, spey,
spey-pyhf, jax, and ROOT (with ROOT.Experimental.XRooFit, i.e.
ROOT >= 6.32.14) for every invocation -- including 'CheckMATE --help'

These modules are only used in CheckMATE2.stateval(), which is reached
only when multibin fits are requested (-mb select|scan|detailed):

- checkmate_core.py: import multibin_limit, multibin_limit_full,
  workspace_calc, spey_wrapper, and hs3_wrapper through a guarded
  _import_optional() helper that records the ImportError and binds the
  name to None instead of failing at startup. Each module is guarded
  individually so that e.g. a missing bleeding-edge ROOT (hs3_wrapper)
  does not disable the pyhf/spey paths. The now redundant Python 3
  version gate around the imports is dropped.
- stateval(): every call into the five modules is preceded by a
  _require_stats() check that aborts via AdvPrint.cerr_exit() with the
  module name, the original ImportError, and an installation hint
  (pyhf / pyhf and jsonpatch / spey and spey-pyhf / ROOT >= 6.32.14
  with XRooFit) when the requested feature is unavailable.
- multibin_limit.py, multibin_limit_full.py: drop the unused
  'import matplotlib.pyplot' (both files) and 'import scipy'
  (multibin_limit.py). matplotlib no longer appears anywhere in the
  dependency surface, so it can be dropped entirely.

A plain CheckMATE run (and AnalysisManager) now only need numpy and
scipy. pyhf, jsonpatch, spey, spey-pyhf, jax, and ROOT/XRooFit are needed
at runtime only when multibin fits are actually requested.

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-fable-5
